ollows the  terrain and interacts with the path and  the scenery and that's in that way it's  sort of an inspiration here even though  the theme is completely different and  the layout is - it's sort of that's real  interactive aspect that I want to get in  here as well I also really want to make  this coaster look charming in a way  which is a really strange sort of goal  to have for a coaster but I don't  exactly want to make something really  impressive or large or epic or anything  like this it's just a sort of small  experiment to make something that's like  small and charming and unique which I  find it's actually the hardest sort of  thing to do not just because what is  charming and what isn't is sort of  subjective and more or less based on my  own judgment here it's your stats making  something really large and impressive  and epic it's just it's still something  you can kind of follow some rules or  guides for but there is no sort of guide  on how to make something look charming  it's just there is no real approach to  it it's really hard to really get that  across and that's what I really am  trying to do with this coaster to make  something that really has its own sort  of signature style and instead of being  like this very large Grande coaster it's  just a small family coaster with some  simple scenery or a simple maybe I do  mix a lot of elements in here but like  nothing that's completely very vast or  massive and yeah make that look just in  a way like a charming little family  coaster that's basically the objective  and in that way I feel like this is much  harder to do then make  and it sort of very large spectacular  ride just because it there is no way to  really get it done right except for what  you sort of feel should be done and what  you sort of feel is right and really  have to kind of follow well your  instincts with that I guess anyway  that's just a little bit of stuff which  I wanted to talk about but I have no  idea what you're actually gonna do with  that information I also wanted to make a  quick steam engine over here which is  not so much like a serious sort of  scenery projects over here but just  something that I quickly wanted to test  as a little prototype to mess around  with the pipes a bit more and try to  make that wheel of the steam engine  especially actually work somehow and of  course also sort of well put the main  theme of this coaster because it is  steampunk and every it revolves around  steam engine technology more or less in  the center sort of focal points of this  entire landscape and it's definitely  gonna be visible from many different  areas so yeah I just wanted to  accentuate this theme and this area with  a little steampunk engine or steam  engine I should say perhaps a bit in a  steampunk ish style it's also something  that I figured would work quite well  since I wanted to have some sort of  scenery piece over here but obviously  since this is right in front of the lift  so I didn't want to make anything that's  very tall  or I would more or less break the  perspective that I have over here so I  just wanted to have something that's  very small  and low but could still work quite well  as a sort of center point scenery piece  here and I think it works quite well to  have this little steampunk machinery  over here in the middle of it and  actually picked up quite a few ideas  that I still have to do on how you can  make some cogs and gears because there  definitely are many ways to get around  that with the current pieces and I might  actually make some pipes out of that  like little wooden piece which I think  should be quite feasible and actually a  good way to get some brass pipes so that  I think that's something I want to mess  around with in the next episode  that's way too early in the video to  talk about that I am running out of the  time apps though but I do still have  some small real-time parts that I do  want to show off a bit to at least show  what the layout looks like in its full  glory at the moment so this is what it  looks like it's not that tall as you can  see it is pretty small but it still goes  on for quite a while and has like really  that sort of higher section a middle  section and the lower section where it  dives underneath the path and this is  what it looked like looks like from the  path area in general with the steam  engine in front of it but there is still  a lot to add like at the moment it looks  quite empty and I really want to add  machinery and rocks and all sorts of  stuff all around the track and not leave  it as bare as it is at the moment and  for a final overview of what it looks  like this is it so thank you guys for  watching and I hope to see you guys in  the next episode
 

